{"type":"document","version":"0.4","doc":"readme","source":"README.md","sha256":"0afdb86ddae8de9cd5d5b8c778609ee6d35a3553b9fc143c1890856764b01045","protection":"none","signed":false,"converter":"fmjl 0.4","structure":true,"elements":25,"created":"2026-09-28T20:11:27Z","lang":"en","access":["all"],"last_id":25}
{"id":"readme#e1","hash":"5636dbcbeadd314d","type":"heading","level":1,"parent":null,"characters":6,"md":"# FMJL"}
{"id":"readme#e2","hash":"aef3f50b2cc4ddfc","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e1","characters":134,"md":"FMJL, short for Format, Markdown, JSON Lines, is a document format that combines four\nlanguages, each doing the one job it is best at:"}
{"id":"readme#e3","hash":"6080d801b6fff20a","type":"table","parent":"readme#e1","characters":670,"md":"| Language | Job in FMJL | Why that one |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| JSON Lines | The container: one element per line, with its id, hash, page, position and permissions | Every programming language reads JSON; one line per element means a file can be streamed, searched and cut without a parser |\n| Markdown | All readable text: headings, paragraphs, lists, simple tables, image descriptions | People can read and write it directly; it is the language of GitHub, VS Code and every editor |\n| LaTeX | Math formulas | The only language that writes every formula exactly |\n| HTML | Tables with merged cells or multi-level headers | Markdown tables cannot merge cells; HTML can |"}
{"id":"readme#e4","hash":"7271c86afe2da66c","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e1","characters":441,"md":"No single format does this on its own. Markdown cannot carry an image's page and position,\ncannot tie a caption to its image, and cannot say who may read a paragraph. JSON can hold\nthose facts but nobody wants to write or read a document as JSON. LaTeX writes formulas\nperfectly but is slow to parse and hard for most people to write. HTML has the tables but\nis heavy everywhere else. FMJL takes the strength of each and leaves the rest out."}
{"id":"readme#e5","hash":"83bb10bd50bb17d5","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e1","characters":412,"md":"A document becomes a list of small parts called elements: headings, paragraphs, lists,\ntables, formulas, code, images, captions, footnotes, form fields, stamps, watermarks and\nmore. Every element has a stable id, a content hash, a page and position, and a permission\nlist. That is what RAG systems and search engines need, and it is why FMJL reads a document\nin about a tenth of a millisecond (see `benchmark/`)."}
{"id":"readme#e6","hash":"51f781aba764f1b8","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e1","characters":58,"md":"One document has two forms that hold the same information:"}
{"id":"readme#e7","hash":"4ce72eb5c51ef077","type":"table","parent":"readme#e1","characters":171,"md":"| Form | File | Made for |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Storage | `name.fmjl` | Machines: search, RAG, databases |\n| Authoring | `name.md` | People: reading, writing, reviewing |"}
{"id":"readme#e8","hash":"fa8248451f55650d","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"readme#e1","characters":16,"md":"## Folder layout"}
{"id":"readme#e9","hash":"28ad5acf85166db8","type":"code","parent":"readme#e8","characters":469,"md":"```text\nfmjl.py          the reference tool (needs Python 3.9+ and: pip install jsonschema)\nrulebook/        the specification, version 0.4, in both forms\nexamples/        a sample document with its images/ folder\nfmjl-vscode/     the VS Code extension: convert, syntax coloring and live checking\nbenchmark/       the same document in FMJL, Markdown, JSON and LaTeX, and the scores\narchive/         older versions (0.1, 0.2), the evaluation, and the first converter\n```"}
{"id":"readme#e10","hash":"625442a45bdce83c","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"readme#e1","characters":15,"md":"## Everyday use"}
{"id":"readme#e11","hash":"123dc75030e7ffe2","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e10","characters":161,"md":"Write a normal Markdown file, then turn it into the storage form. The command is\n`fmjl <input> <output>`; the file extensions tell the tool which way to convert:"}
{"id":"readme#e12","hash":"c3a086daa272766e","type":"code","parent":"readme#e10","characters":324,"md":"```powershell\nfmjl notes.md  store\\notes.fmjl    # Markdown to storage form, then checks it\nfmjl store\\notes.fmjl  notes.md    # storage form back to Markdown; ids are kept\nfmjl notes.md                      # output left out: notes.fmjl next to the input\nfmjl notes.fmjl                    # same shortcut the other way\n```"}
{"id":"readme#e13","hash":"9e1dbe36ddc703ef","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e10","characters":167,"md":"`fmjl` is the small `fmjl.cmd` file in this folder. Add the folder to your PATH once and\nthe word works from anywhere. Without it, write `python fmjl.py new notes.md`."}
{"id":"readme#e14","hash":"77bd1352c981a4c2","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e10","characters":13,"md":"All commands:"}
{"id":"readme#e15","hash":"98e4a77c7f68da68","type":"table","parent":"readme#e10","characters":609,"md":"| Command | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| `python fmjl.py new notes.md` | Authoring form to storage form |\n| `python fmjl.py md notes.fmjl` | Storage form to authoring form |\n| `python fmjl.py fill notes.fmjl` | Fills in `id`, `hash`, `characters` and `parent`; makes `md` canonical |\n| `python fmjl.py check notes.fmjl` | Checks every rule of the rulebook |\n| `python fmjl.py view notes.fmjl` | Prints the document as clean Markdown |\n| `python fmjl.py info notes.fmjl` | Prints the title, element counts and an outline |\n| `python fmjl.py upgrade old.fmjl` | Turns a version 0.1, 0.2 or 0.3 file into 0.4 |"}
{"id":"readme#e16","hash":"8a0c868b4488af82","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"readme#e1","characters":27,"md":"## What the benchmark shows"}
{"id":"readme#e17","hash":"76e9c313cc2bbf6c","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e16","characters":179,"md":"The same 75-sentence report with two formulas, a table, an image and a caption was written\nin FMJL, Markdown, JSON and LaTeX, then read back and scored (`benchmark/results.json`):"}
{"id":"readme#e18","hash":"e38dc600824f542f","type":"table","parent":"readme#e16","characters":383,"md":"|  | FMJL | Markdown | JSON | LaTeX |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Page number of every element | 23/23 | 0/23 | 23/23 | 0/23 |\n| Caption linked to its image | yes | no | yes | yes |\n| Elements keeping their id after an edit | 23/23 | 0/23 | 21/23 | 5/23 |\n| Detects a silently changed letter | yes | no | no | no |\n| Read one document | 0.11 ms | 3.85 ms | 0.07 ms | 29.32 ms |"}
{"id":"readme#e19","hash":"3057bc0b6faea60d","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"readme#e1","characters":10,"md":"## VS Code"}
{"id":"readme#e20","hash":"ddc6d1b8379462f5","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e19","characters":340,"md":"Search for **FMJL** in the Extensions view and install it (publisher rupakkumar). It needs\nno Python. Right-click a `.md` file for **FMJL: Convert Markdown to .fmjl**, or a `.fmjl`\nfile for **FMJL: Convert .fmjl to Markdown**. Any `.fmjl` file gets coloring, red\nunderlines for rule violations, and the command **FMJL: Check current file**."}
{"id":"readme#e21","hash":"bac802355b0c1efc","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e19","characters":185,"md":"The extension's converter is a JavaScript port of `fmjl.py`. Running\n`node fmjl-vscode/test/roundtrip.js` proves the two give byte-identical output on every\ndocument in this repository."}
{"id":"readme#e22","hash":"3a8c9ed140cb0af3","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"readme#e1","characters":9,"md":"## Status"}
{"id":"readme#e23","hash":"874e45fa8330b186","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e22","characters":110,"md":"Draft, version 0.4. The rulebook is the authority; if `fmjl.py` and the rulebook\ndisagree, the tool has a bug."}
{"id":"readme#e24","hash":"dbe8a79f5ca44487","type":"heading","level":2,"parent":"readme#e1","characters":21,"md":"## Author and license"}
{"id":"readme#e25","hash":"1107522817795559","type":"paragraph","parent":"readme#e24","characters":194,"md":"Created by Rupak Kumar. Released under the MIT License (see `LICENSE`): use it freely,\nkeep the copyright line. Suggestions and bug reports go to\nhttps://github.com/rupakkumar-76319/fmjl/issues."}
